    {
      "id": "p0020-b002",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Every language has its own unique set of colorful phrases that have a literal meaning and a functional meaning. For example, the English phrase \"I'm in a pickle\" literally means \"I am inside of a pickle\" but functionally means \"I'm in a difficult situation\".",
        "raw": "Every language has its own unique set\nof colorful phrases that have a literal\nmeaning and a functional meaning.\nFor example, the English phrase \"I'm\nin a pickle\" literally means \"I am\ninside of a pickle\" but functionally\nmeans \"I'm in a difficult situation\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28577632,
          0.09185714,
          0.57327725,
          0.21378571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28405172,
          0.09114286,
          0.57723368,
          0.21521429
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          2,
          3,
          5,
          8,
          9,
          10,
          11
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "每种语言都有一套生动的说法，既有字面意思，也有实际含义。例如英语 I’m in a pickle，字面是“我在一根酸黄瓜里”，实际却是“我陷入了困境”。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
